📘 Kubeflow Setup Guide (End-to-End)
🧱 1. Prerequisites
Infrastructure
3 VMs:
1 Master (Control Plane)
2 Workers
OS: Ubuntu 22.04 / 24.04
Required Setup
Kubernetes (kubeadm)
Container runtime: containerd
CNI: Calico
Verify Cluster
kubectl get nodes -o wide

✔ Output:

master    Ready
worker1   Ready
worker2   Ready
📦 2. Clone Kubeflow Manifests
git clone https://github.com/kubeflow/manifests.git
cd manifests

(Optional – recommended stable version)

git checkout v1.9.0
⚙️ 3. Install Kubeflow (Correct Method)

❗ IMPORTANT: Do NOT use kubectl apply -k .

✅ Use this command:
while ! kustomize build example | kubectl apply -f -; do
  echo "Retrying..."
  sleep 10
done
⏳ Installation Time
20 – 40 minutes
🔁 What happens during install
Some resources fail initially ❗
Webhooks not ready ❗
CRDs missing ❗

✔ Loop retries until everything succeeds

🔍 4. Monitor Installation
kubectl get pods -A -w
⚠️ 5. Fix Common CrashLoop Issues

After install, some pods may fail (common in local setups).

🔧 Scale down problematic components
# Knative
kubectl scale deployment net-istio-controller -n knative-serving --replicas=0
kubectl scale deployment net-istio-webhook -n knative-serving --replicas=0

# Spark
kubectl scale deployment spark-operator-webhook -n kubeflow --replicas=0

# Metadata
kubectl scale deployment metadata-grpc-deployment -n kubeflow --replicas=0
kubectl scale deployment metadata-writer -n kubeflow --replicas=0

# Training controllers
kubectl scale deployment kubeflow-trainer-controller-manager -n kubeflow-system --replicas=0
kubectl scale deployment jobset-controller-manager -n kubeflow-system --replicas=0

# LLM controller
kubectl scale deployment llmisvc-controller-manager -n kubeflow --replicas=0
✅ Verify
kubectl get pods -A | grep CrashLoopBackOff

✔ Output should be empty

🌐 6. Access Kubeflow Dashboard
Check Istio Gateway
kubectl get svc -n istio-system istio-ingressgateway
Port-forward (on master)
kubectl port-forward svc/istio-ingressgateway -n istio-system 8085:80
